# Mobile screen images and flows

Generate images only, not SwiftUI, React Native, Flutter, HTML or implementation prose. Check the available image-generation capability; disclose missing capability instead of claiming an image was generated.

## Essential contract

1. Decide iOS, Android or cross-platform mode first. Respect safe areas, system regions, native navigation and platform conventions; do not casually mix platforms.
2. Build one app design bible: palette roles, type scale, spacing/radii, icon/media treatment, navigation, background texture and device framing. Preserve the same system across screens while varying layouts according to each screen's purpose.
3. Generate the requested number of readable standalone screens and a logical flow. More detail views are justified when extraction/readability requires them; do not substitute a vague compressed idea board. Generate fresh dedicated details rather than cropping an old image.
4. Default to a subtle premium phone mockup with visible consistent frame and even margins. Content remains the hero; the device must not dominate, clip, warp or shrink screen text. Use a bare-screen exception only when the user requests it.
5. Keep first screens comprehensible, controls legible, contrast usable, tap/navigation affordances plausible, and short copy meaningful. Do not invent decorative charts, fake system complexity or code output.
6. Inspect consistency, flow and quality before delivery; regenerate weak screens/details and label the complete set. User-approved style overrides art-direction defaults.

